      "created_at": "2017-07-04T13:43:50.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Okay, I'm kidding. &nbsp;But seriously, there are several discrepancies in their bios. &nbsp;Names are different, birthplace is different, eyecolor is different.Most damning of all, they have different skin tones. &nbsp;Eye color changes are common. &nbsp;Names can be changed. &nbsp;Birthplace can be a matter of perspective if something \"made me a new man\". &nbsp;But a skin-color change from one natural shade to another? &nbsp;When was the last time you saw that happen?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It was a wild theory thought up in a somewhat buzzed hazed late at night before bed.</p>\n<p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name and birthplace: He didn't want to be associated with his unscrupulous past, so he changed it.</p>\n<p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Eye colour: Some people's eyes change colour with age</p>\n<p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; And for that skin colour, maybe being in Insula Primalis, and hanging around Citizen Hammer just gave him a wicked tan!&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The stone he carries is a source of great power.</p>\n<p>-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Also, the legend that is Christopher is the used for the art for Citizen Anvil. The variant for Scholar wears a vest. Christopher likes (loves?) vests….</p>\n<p>COINCIDENCE?!</p>\n<p>Yes. I'm pretty sure these are all coincidences</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
