      "raw": "[quote=\"Arcanist Lupus\"]\n\nYes.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Okay, I&#39;m kidding. &nbsp;But seriously, there are several discrepancies in their bios. &nbsp;Names are different, birthplace is different, eyecolor is different.Most damning of all, they have different skin tones. &nbsp;Eye color changes are common. &nbsp;Names can be changed. &nbsp;Birthplace can be a matter of perspective if something &quot;made me a new man&quot;. &nbsp;But a skin-color change from one natural shade to another? &nbsp;When was the last time you saw that happen?\n\n[/quote]\n\nIt was a wild theory thought up in a somewhat buzzed hazed late at night before bed.\n\n-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Name and birthplace: He didn&#39;t want to be associated with his unscrupulous past, so he changed it.\n\n-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Eye colour: Some people&#39;s eyes change colour with age\n\n-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; And for that skin colour, maybe being in Insula Primalis, and hanging around Citizen Hammer just gave him a wicked tan!&nbsp;\n\n-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The stone he carries is a source of great power.\n\n-&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Also, the legend that is Christopher is the used for the art for Citizen Anvil. The variant for Scholar wears a vest. Christopher likes (loves?) vests&hellip;.\n\nCOINCIDENCE?!\n\nYes. I&#39;m pretty sure these are all coincidences\n\n&nbsp;\n",
